# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FRONTEND (.env) — every VITE_ var below is PUBLIC.
#
# Vite inlines VITE_-prefixed vars into the JS bundle at build time. Anyone can
# read them with devtools. NEVER put an API key, token, or secret here.
# Secrets belong in the Worker — see the backend section.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the optimize endpoint lives.
#   Same-origin (Cloudflare routes dipayan.shop/api/* to the Worker):
VITE_API_BASE="/api"
#   Standalone Worker (no custom-domain routing) — remember to add your site's
#   origin to ALLOWED_ORIGINS in wrangler.toml:
# VITE_API_BASE="https://prompt-optimiser-api.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev"
#   Empty builds a fully offline app that only uses the in-browser rule-based
#   optimizer:
# VITE_API_BASE=""


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BACKEND (Cloudflare Worker)
#
# Non-secret config lives in [vars] in wrangler.toml.
# Secrets are set with `npx wrangler secret put <NAME>` and never committed.
# For local `wrangler dev`, put secrets in .dev.vars (gitignored) — not here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# GROQ_API_KEY   — free tier key: https://console.groq.com/keys
#                  Production: npx wrangler secret put GROQ_API_KEY
#                  Local dev:  echo 'GROQ_API_KEY="gsk_..."' >> .dev.vars

# MODEL_BACKEND  — auto | groq | workers-ai | ollama | rule-based
#                  Unset defaults to `auto`, which is what production wants.

# Local Ollama only (MODEL_BACKEND=ollama). See docker-compose.yml / `make ollama`.
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL="http://localhost:11434"
# OLLAMA_MODEL="llama3.1:8b"
